## [007] Component inventory

```
app/
  layout.tsx            Fonts, metadata, sticky chrome, Lenis mount, footer
  page.tsx              Composition; maps activeServiceLines() in canonical order
  globals.css           Tailwind v4 @theme, brand tokens, reveal + Lenis CSS
lib/
  content.ts            SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
components/
  SmoothScroll.tsx      Lenis + anchor interception (client)
  Reveal.tsx            One-shot entrance reveal (client)
  PriceLockup.tsx       Universal price renderer
  CallCta.tsx           Every tel: link; owns data-call-cta and label rules
  Logo.tsx              Original retailer wordmark in the GFiber palette
  icons.tsx             Inline SVG set, no icon dependency
  TopDisclosureBar.tsx  Persistent disclosure
  Header.tsx            Sticky header, anchor nav, call button (client)
  Hero.tsx              Eyebrow, H1, subline, ZIP + call, trust chips, price anchor
  ZipChecker.tsx        Client-side ZIP validation, routes to phone (client)
  PlanCard.tsx          Stacked and wide variants
  ServiceSection.tsx    Generic service-line renderer; null when empty
  FinePrintGrid.tsx     Table at md+, stacked cards below
  WhyFiber.tsx          Dark features section
  HowItWorks.tsx        Three-step ordering section
  Faq.tsx               Native <details> accordion, no client JS
  Footer.tsx            Dark footer, 8 mandatory legal links, disclosures
```

Client components are limited to the four that genuinely need browser APIs
(`SmoothScroll`, `Reveal`, `Header`, `ZipChecker`). Everything else is a server
component, so almost no JavaScript ships for the content itself.

---

## [008] Responsive and accessibility guarantees

- `html, body { overflow-x: clip }` plus `min-w-0` on every grid child — no
  horizontal overflow at 320px.
- The fine-print table is replaced by stacked cards below `md` rather than
  scrolled sideways.
- `scroll-margin-top: 7.5rem` on `[id]` clears the disclosure bar + header.
- Native `<details>` FAQ — keyboard and screen-reader behaviour from the browser.
- Skip link to `#plans`.
- Visible focus ring on every interactive element, on light and dark surfaces.
- All motion collapses under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, including Lenis.

---

## [009] Bundles refactored to composed pricing

**Problem found during verification.** Bundle plans stored their monthly rate as
a literal (`price: 90`) and restated their parts in text (`"1 Gig at $70 plus
Home Phone at $20"`). Changing the 1 Gig rate in one place would therefore have
left every bundle containing it showing a stale price — a real break in the
single-source-of-truth guarantee.

**Fix.** A bundle is now a composition, not a price. `BundleSpec` names an
internet plan id plus add-on plan ids; `composeBundle()` derives the monthly
rate, the cents, both speeds, the data policy, the contract term, the install
line and the "X at $70 plus Y at $20" qualifier from the referenced plans.
`requirePlan()` throws at module load if a spec points at an unknown id, so a
typo fails the build instead of shipping a wrong price.

Catalogue assembly is now:

```
fiberPlans ─┐
            ├─ basePlans ─→ composeBundle() ─→ bundlePlans
phonePlans ─┘                                        │
                                                     ▼
            plans = [...fiberPlans, ...bundlePlans, ...phonePlans]
```

---

## [010] 320px header fix

**Problem found during verification.** At a 320px viewport the header's call
button extended to 372px — 52px past the viewport. `overflow-x: clip` meant the
page could not be scrolled sideways, so the defect surfaced as the primary CTA
being visually cut off rather than as a scrollbar.

**Fix.** Below the `sm` breakpoint the logo mark drops to 28px, the wordmark and
retailer qualifier step down a size, and the header call button loses its icon
and tightens to `px-3 py-2 text-xs`. The button's right edge now lands at 304px
inside a 320px viewport, clearing the 16px gutter. Nothing changes at `sm` and
above.

