## [014] Hero rebuilt; copy raised to a professional register

**Hero.** The bordered form card around the availability checker read as a
generic template. It is gone. The checker is now a single elevated pill —
the same pattern Google Fiber uses for its own address bar — with an sr-only
label, an inline pin icon and a solid `#008064` submit. Supporting changes:
larger display scale (up to 3.75rem), a mint/orange radial wash, refined trust
markers, and a restyled price card with the tier hairline.

**Removed at the operator's request:**

- The `Call to order` button and the "Prefer to talk it through…" helper
  paragraph inside the hero availability card.
- The "Order by phone / Mon-Fri 8am-9pm ET" block in the navbar.

> The hero still satisfies the hard requirement to carry **both** a ZIP checker
> and a call button: the ZIP pill remains, and the `Call to order` button on the
> lead-plan price card is untouched. Verified live — hero contains one
> `data-call-cta` link plus the postal-code input. The hours line survives in
> the footer, which was not in scope for removal.

**Copy rewritten to a professional register** (all in `lib/content.ts`):

| Before                                          | After                                       |
| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Multi-gig fiber, at a price that holds.         | Multi-gigabit fiber, engineered for the modern home. |
| Internet and home phone together                | Complete home connectivity                  |
| Hardware, fees and what is actually included    | Transparent pricing, itemized               |
| What a pure fiber network actually changes      | The advantage of end-to-end fiber           |
| Three steps to a scheduled install              | From availability check to installation     |
| Questions we get before an order                | Common questions, answered                  |

Supporting sublines were rewritten to match, and the fiber/phone section
subheadings were tightened.

**New shared component — `SectionHeading.tsx`.** Every section now renders its
eyebrow, heading and subheading through one component, so the accent rule,
display size (40px), tracking (-1.4px) and 112px vertical rhythm are identical
down the page. Verified live across all seven sections.

