## [015] Tailwind v4 important-modifier bug

`Header` and `ZipChecker` sized their CTAs with v3-style important prefixes
(`!px-3`, `sm:!px-5`, `!py-3`). **Tailwind v4 moved the important modifier to a
suffix (`px-3!`)**, so every one of those classes was dead — the buttons were
silently falling back to base padding.

Fixed at the source rather than by rewriting the classes: `CallCta` now owns a
`size` prop (`sm | md`) and no caller passes sizing overrides. Confirmed at
320px after a hard reload — header CTA computes 12px padding and 12px type,
right edge at 304px inside a 320px viewport, 16px gutter intact, zero
horizontal overflow and zero non-decorative elements past the edge.

**Re-audit after the redesign:** 11 `tel:` links with 0 missing
`data-call-cta`; 9 "Call to order" and 0 "Call for pricing"; raw phone as button
text exactly twice (header + footer); 8/8 legal links; all forbidden strings 0;
section order unchanged; `#cable`, `#tv`, `#mobile` still absent. Link and CTA
counts dropped by one each because the hero CTA removal above was intentional.
`tsc` clean · `eslint` clean · `next build` static.

