## [016] Hero re-architected as a centred stack; spacing tightened

**The split layout was the problem.** The previous hero used the common
"copy left / product card right" arrangement. That pattern — not the styling of
the card — is what read as a generic template.

Checked against the references: Google Fiber's own hero, bestfiberinternet.us
and kineticfiber.us all lead with a **single centred column**. The hero now
follows that: centred eyebrow, headline, subline, availability pill and trust
markers, with no floating panel.

**The price anchor moved to a horizontal band.** The dark lead-plan card is
gone. The `<PriceLockup />` requirement is now carried by a slim full-width
lockup below the trust markers: tier dot, plan name, price, `Call to order`,
and a tinted promo row beneath. It stacks to a column below `sm`.

`PriceLockup` gained `showQualifier` so the band does not repeat the promo line
that its own footer row already states.

> The hero still carries **both** required elements — verified live: one
> postal-code input and one `data-call-cta` link.

**Spacing.** Two separate gaps were called out and both were measured before
and after:

| Gap                                  | Before | After |
| ------------------------------------ | ------ | ----- |
| Navbar bottom → hero eyebrow          | 112px  | 58px  |
| Hero price band → plans heading       | 152px  | 80px  |

Hero padding went to `pt-10 pb-10 / sm:pt-12 sm:pb-12 / lg:pt-14`. Every
section container moved from `py-20 sm:py-24 lg:py-28` to
`py-14 sm:py-16 lg:py-20`. Hero height dropped 825px → 739px.

Most of the dead space in the second screenshot came from the old grid being
`items-center` with a tall right-hand card, which left the shorter left column
padded out. Removing the card removed that entirely.

**Copy, second revision:**

| Before                                               | After                                        |
| ---------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Multi-gigabit fiber, engineered for the modern home. | Pure fiber. Symmetrical speed. Fixed pricing. |
| Transparent pricing, itemized                        | Equipment, fees and inclusions                |

**Verified:** 320px → 0px horizontal overflow, zero non-decorative offenders,
price band stacks to a column with its 16px gutter intact, H1 scales to 40px.
0 `tel:` links missing `data-call-cta`; 9 "Call to order"; 8/8 legal links.
`tsc` clean · `eslint` clean · `next build` static.

