## [018] Hero scrim removed; offer promoted; two sections rebuilt

### Hero backdrop scrim removed

The white gradient over the hero photograph is gone. Only a 7rem fade remains at
the very bottom so the section edge meets the next one cleanly.

**This broke text contrast, and the fix was to darken the text rather than put
the scrim back.** Measured against the actual photograph by sampling the
rendered pixels behind the subline:

| Element  | Colour  | Before | After |
| -------- | ------- | ------ | ----- |
| Headline | `#202124` | 8.89:1 | 8.89:1 (unchanged, already passing) |
| Subline  | `#5F6368` → `#3C4043` | **3.34:1 — failed AA** | **5.74:1 — passes** |

A new token `--color-gf-slate-dark: #3C4043` (Google grey 800) was added for
body text sitting over photography. Both hero text elements also carry a faint
white text-shadow for edge definition against the image — that is an outline on
the glyphs, not a layer over the picture.

### Offer given real prominence

`hero.promoHighlight` was a quiet line in the price band footer. It is replaced
by a dedicated `offer` object in `lib/content.ts` (`badge`, `headline`,
`detail`) rendered as a solid `#008064` bar across the **top** of the price
band, with a badge and the headline in white. The terms stay in the tinted row
beneath the lockup.

`hero.promoHighlight` was deleted rather than left unused — dead data invites
someone to edit it and wonder why nothing changes.

### Plan photography moved to the top of the card

Images now lead each card instead of closing it. Giving the card a subject
before it gives a number is what stops a pricing grid reading as a spreadsheet.
The tier accent bar gained `z-10` so it still renders above the photograph,
which creates its own stacking context once it sits first.

The wide (single-plan) card variant now supports an image too, as a 3:1 banner.

### Why Fiber rebuilt

Four equal icon tiles is the most over-used section pattern on the web. Replaced
with an editorial layout: the fiber macro is now a real captioned `<figure>` on
the left, and the four points run as a numbered `01–04` list separated by
hairlines on the right. **Zero card boxes remain** — verified in the DOM.

### How It Works rebuilt

Deliberately given a different shape from Why Fiber so the two never read as the
same block twice. Heading sits beside the installation photograph, then the
three steps run left-to-right along a hairline rule with `01–03` markers, and
the section closes on a CTA row carrying the agent hours.

### Headline, third revision

`Pure fiber. Symmetrical speed. Fixed pricing.` →
**`Multi-gigabit fiber internet, direct to your home.`**
("pure" and "fixed" ruled out by the operator.)

Fine-print heading: `Transparent pricing, itemized` →
**`Equipment, fees and inclusions`**.

### Still outstanding

The Home Phone card has no photograph — no such file was supplied. The slot is
wired and renders nothing rather than a placeholder, so dropping
`public/images/plan-phone.jpg` in and adding the import is all that is needed. A
prompt for it is appended to `IMAGE-BRIEF.md` as image 8 (3:1 banner, landline
handset rather than a mobile, since the product is a home line).

### Verified

- Hero subline 5.74:1 against the live photograph, scrim confirmed absent.
- All three fiber cards: image above the title, full-bleed, CTA below.
- Why Fiber: figure + caption, items `01–04`, 0 card boxes.
- How It Works: 3-column flow, steps `01–03`, connecting rule, closing CTA.
- Offer bar stacks to a column at 320px and fits the viewport.
- 320px: 0px horizontal overflow, zero non-decorative offenders, card image
  flush inside the card border.
- `tsc` clean · `eslint` clean · `next build` static and warning-free.

