## [020] Hero re-lit; ambient motion added across the site

The operator's note was that the hero read dull, the headline had no weight and
the photograph was not really visible. Three separate causes.

> **Brief change.** Entry [002] set a deliberately small motion budget. The
> operator has since asked for vibrant animated gradient backgrounds, so that
> constraint is superseded. The still-standing exclusions from the original
> brief — no WebGL, no 3D spirals, no animated assembly diagrams — are intact.

### 1. The photograph was flat, not dark

Measured: channel stdev ~58–66 on a 0–255 range, which is a genuinely
low-contrast frame. Graded with sharp — saturation ×1.42, linear contrast
1.22x−26, gamma 1.05, light sharpen. Stdev now 66–76 and the greens and wood
read properly. 82 KB → 109 KB. Ungraded originals are backed up in the session
scratchpad.

### 2. The scrim was doing the damage

Entry [018] removed the white scrim, but the rebuild reintroduced one as a
"bloom" at `rgba(255,255,255,0.78)` over the centre — the same mistake wearing a
different name. Cut to `0.30`, at which point the room is clearly legible.

### 3. The headline had no weight

Now `font-bold` at up to 4.25rem with tighter `-0.04em` tracking, and the
closing phrase carries a brand-teal gradient. The headline is stored in
`lib/content.ts` as `headlineLead` + `headlineAccent`, with `headline` derived
from both so metadata keeps the full string.

**Two real bugs found and fixed while doing this:**

- **`text-shadow` bleeds through `bg-clip-text`.** The white glow painted behind
  the glyphs shows straight through the transparent fill, washing the gradient
  to a pale mint. Switched to `drop-shadow`, which respects the alpha mask.
- **The gradient failed contrast.** Its light stop `#008064` measured
  **2.52:1** against the photograph — below even the 3:1 large-text minimum.
  Regraded to run `#004A3C → #005D4A → #004A3C`; the lightest stop now measures
  **4.01:1**, clearing the normal-text threshold, not just the large-text one.

Final measured contrast over the live photograph: headline **8.20:1**,
accent **4.01:1**, subline **6.03:1**.

### Ambient motion

`components/AuroraBackdrop.tsx` — two or three large blurred blobs in the tier
accents (`#00BE8E`, `#FF7321`, `#FF72FC`) drifting on independent 22/28/34s
loops, in `light`, `vivid` and `dark` intensities. Applied to all eight
sections.

Also added: a 30s Ken Burns push-in on the hero photograph, a 12s hue pan on the
teal→orange→magenta brand rules, a shimmer sweep across the offer bar, and a
pulse ring on the eyebrow dot.

**Performance shape:** only `transform` and `background-position` animate, so
blurred layers rasterise once and are then moved by the compositor rather than
re-blurred each frame. Blur radius is 56px and the `light` variant uses two
blobs rather than three, taking the page from 24 blurred layers to 18.

`contain: paint` was tried on the blobs and **removed** — it clips painting to
the element box, which would cut the blur halo off at a hard edge.

Everything stops under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; the guard was confirmed
present in the live CSSOM covering all seven animated classes.

### Verified

- 24 animations running, all in `running` state; aurora present on all 8 sections.
- Reduced-motion guard found in the served stylesheet.
- 320px: `documentScrollWidth` 320, 0px overflow, cannot scroll sideways, and
  zero overflowing text or controls once elements safely clipped by an
  `overflow:hidden` ancestor are excluded.
- `tsc` clean · `eslint` clean · `next build` static and warning-free.

### Not verified

Frame rate under animation could not be measured — `requestAnimationFrame` is
throttled while the preview pane is hidden, so the probe never returned. The
design is transform-only for this reason, but an FPS reading on a real device
has not been taken.

---

## [021] Fiber-flow background and headline motion

### `components/FiberFlow.tsx`

Light travelling along fiber strands — the one background motif that is
literally the product rather than generic decoration.

Four curved paths drawn twice each: a faint static strand, and over it a heavily
dashed stroke whose `stroke-dashoffset` animates, so a single lit segment runs
the length of the curve. Dash pattern is `230 <pathLength>`, so exactly one
pulse occupies a strand at a time. Speeds 9/11/13/15s with staggered delays, in
`#00BE8E`, `#00D699`, `#FF7321` and `#FF72FC`, through an SVG Gaussian-blur glow
filter. Five junction nodes blip on their own 3.2–5.1s cycles.

**Two fixes during tuning:**

- `preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"` cropped to roughly the middle 50% of
  the composition on a tall hero, hiding most of the strands. Changed to `none`
  — these are abstract curves, so stretching costs nothing and keeps them all on
  screen.
- Strands were invisible over the photograph at the first settings. Static
  opacity 0.16 → 0.28, pulse dash 120 → 230, stroke +0.5, layer opacity
  0.7 → 0.9, plus `vectorEffect="non-scaling-stroke"` so the stretch does not
  thin the lines.

### Headline

- **Colour flow** — the accent phrase is filled with a five-stop gradient at
  `background-size: 230%`, panning on a 9s cycle.
- **Glow** — a breathing teal bloom behind the headline on a 7s cycle. It sits
  *behind* the glyphs, so it adds light without touching text contrast, and is
  ordered before the `<h1>` at default z-index; a negative z-index dropped it
  behind the photograph instead.

**Contrast under animation.** Because the fill now moves, every stop has to
hold, not just one. Measured against the live photograph:

| Stop | Ratio |
| ---- | ----- |
| `#00604E` (lightest) | 3.85:1 |
| `#005D4A` | 4.02:1 |
| `#004A3C` | 5.24:1 |

All clear the 3:1 large-text minimum at 68px/700, and the two darker stops clear
4.5:1 outright. Headline 8.21:1, subline 6.03:1.

A brighter "shine" band sweeping through the text was tried and **rejected** —
it dropped glyphs to roughly 2.5:1 as it passed. The glow behind the text gives
the same impression without the contrast cost.

### Verified

39 animations running; fiber SVG present with 4 flow paths; reduced-motion guard
extended to `.gf-flow`, `.gf-node`, `.gf-text-flow` and `.gf-breathe`, with
`.gf-flow` pinned to `stroke-dashoffset: 0` so a lit segment stays visible
rather than leaving a bare line. 320px: 0px horizontal overflow, no sideways
scroll, zero overflowing content. `tsc` clean · `eslint` clean · `next build`
static and warning-free.

