## [022] Mobile responsiveness pass; repository and Vercel readiness

### Touch targets

Audited every interactive element at 320 / 375 / 768 / 1440. Three failures, all
fixed:

| Element | Before | After |
| ------- | ------ | ----- |
| Footer links (16 of them) | 17px | 40px |
| Header call CTA | 32px | 44px |
| Header nav links (tablet and up) | 23px | 47px |

Footer links were bare inline text; they are now `block` with vertical padding,
and the list gaps were tightened so the column reads at roughly its previous
density rather than growing. `CallCta` carries a `min-h-11` floor at both sizes.

### Motion budget on phones

Phones do the same compositing work on a fraction of the GPU and on battery, so
a `max-width: 767px` block trims the expensive parts while keeping the effect:

- blur radius 56px → 38px
- third aurora blob hidden (18 → 16 layers)
- two of the four fiber strands hidden (`gf-flow-secondary`)
- the SVG Gaussian-blur glow on strands and nodes disabled — the costliest part

Live animation count drops from 39 to 35 at phone width, with materially less
per-layer cost.

### Verified across breakpoints

| Width | Overflow | Layout | Small targets |
| ----- | -------- | ------ | ------------- |
| 320px | 0px | 1-col cards, table → stacked | none |
| 375px | 0px | 1-col cards | none |
| 768px | 0px | 2-col cards, table restored | none |
| 1440px | 0px | 3-col cards, 2-col Why Fiber, 3-col flow | none |

Type scales 40 → 68px (h1) and 30 → 40px (h2) across that range.

### Repository

Initialised and pushed to `github.com/PavithraEbbali/googlefiber`, branch `main`,
commit `74aa352`, 44 files. Remote ref verified to match local HEAD.

Removed before committing: a leftover `wm-after.jpg` scratch file from the
watermark work, and the five unused create-next-app scaffold SVGs
(`file/globe/next/vercel/window.svg`) — confirmed zero references first.
Scanned for credentials; none present and no `.env` files exist.

`gh` CLI is not installed on this machine; the push went through Git Credential
Manager, which was already configured.

### Vercel

No `vercel.json` is needed — Next.js is auto-detected. `README.md` documents the
one required environment variable, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`, without which social
crawlers are handed a placeholder host for the OpenGraph image.

### Known cosmetic build warning

`next build` reports `Unknown at rule: @theme` against `app/globals.css`.
Turbopack's CSS parser inspects the file before PostCSS hands it to Tailwind v4,
which owns that at-rule. Verified non-functional by confirming the compiled
stylesheet contains every brand token, all five keyframe sets, the three
reduced-motion guards and the 767px mobile guard. No action taken.

