## [023] Deployment broke — restoring build config deleted in [022]

The Vercel deployment rendered with **no CSS at all**: an unconstrained logo SVG
filling the viewport, its `fill-gf-teal` rect falling back to black.

### Cause — self-inflicted

The cleanup in [022] removed scratch files with this glob:

```
rm -f ... zoom.jpg opt_*.img t.img *.mjs
```

`*.mjs` was meant for the throwaway image scripts. It also matched
**`postcss.config.mjs`** and **`eslint.config.mjs`**, the two root config files.
Without the PostCSS config, Tailwind never runs, so the build emits no
stylesheet — and because the deletion happened before `git add`, the broken
state was what got pushed.

### Why it was not caught

Two compounding verification failures, both mine:

1. **Verified the wrong artifact.** The check for brand tokens and keyframes ran
   against `.next/dev/static/...` — development output, and stale output at
   that, generated before the deletion. The production bundle in `.next/static`
   was never inspected. Dev kept serving cached CSS, so the local site looked
   fine throughout.
2. **Dismissed the actual signal.** `next build` reported
   `Unknown at rule: @theme` and this was written off as a cosmetic Turbopack
   parser quirk. It was not. Turbopack saw a raw `@theme` because Tailwind had
   never processed the file — the warning *was* the bug reporting itself. It
   disappeared the moment the PostCSS config was restored.

A third, smaller issue: lint checks had been running as
`npx eslint . --ext .ts,.tsx | tail -5 && echo "LINT OK"`. Piping into `tail`
makes the pipeline exit status that of `tail`, so "LINT OK" printed
unconditionally — and `--ext` is not valid in ESLint 9 flat config anyway. Those
runs proved nothing.

### Fix

- `postcss.config.mjs` restored.
- `eslint.config.mjs` rewritten. The first restoration attempt used `FlatCompat`
  and crashed with a circular-reference error; `eslint-config-next@16` ships
  native flat configs, so it now imports `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals`
  and `eslint-config-next/typescript` directly.

### Verified against the production build this time

- `.next/static/chunks/*.css` — **53,959 bytes** (previously absent).
- All nine brand tokens present; `bg-gf-teal`, `fill-gf-teal`,
  `text-gf-charcoal`, `gf-display`, `gf-eyebrow`, `min-h-11` all generated.
- All seven keyframe sets, the reduced-motion guard and the 767px mobile guard
  present.
- `next build` now emits **no warnings**.
- Served the production build with `next start` and confirmed the stylesheet is
  linked in the HTML, returns 200, and the page renders correctly.
- `eslint` exit code 0 with the status no longer masked by a pipe; `tsc` exit 0.
